{
  "v": "stozher/0.1",
  "kind": "catalog",
  "catalog-version": "2026.07.1",
  "description": "Tier B — the curated server+tool to action+class catalog shipped with the product (spec 08 section 5, spec 10 section 3). Org policy reclassification applies on top of every entry, in both directions; nothing here is final, and a shipped entry is never silently replaced by an org-seeded one.",
  "class-notes": {
    "read": "retrieves state and applies nothing. Exfiltration is a read, which is why reads are still recorded — folded into aggregation records rather than dropped.",
    "benign": "applies an effect with no consequence outside the caller's own session. A heuristic may never assign this; it takes shipped curation or a manifest.",
    "consequential": "changes state a human would want to have approved: writes, sends, merges, spends, grants. Anything that spawns another agent is consequential, because the sub-agent's effects are real.",
    "prohibited": "hard-blocked by policy whatever the mandate says. Deliberately almost empty here: an organization states its own prohibitions, and a vendor default that quietly forbids things is a vendor making policy."
  },
